# QA Compatibility Wrapper

Use this only when the request says "QA" generically. Route immediately into the canonical testing surface.

## Modes

| Mode | Skill | When to Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ui-harness` | `qa` | Making the routing decision for a broad QA request |
| `web` | `web-testing` | Running browser QA through Playwright MCP and the canonical web-testing skill |
| `android` | `android-emulator-testing` | Running Android emulator QA through the CLI-first Android testing skill |
| `ios` | `ios-simulator-testing` | Running iOS simulator QA through the CLI-first iOS testing skill |

## Code-level Testing

Do not route code-level unit or integration coverage here. Load the language or framework skill that owns the code under test and keep testing guidance with that stack.

## Skill References

- `qa`
- `web-testing`
- `android-emulator-testing`
- `ios-simulator-testing`
